            <ArticleTitle>Case 11: large, infected, necrotic mixed-aetiology leg ulcer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S19</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.12968/jowc.2016.25.Sup3.S19</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This painful and malodorous ulcer was covered with 40% necrotic tissue. Combined use of octenilin Wound gel and Wound Irrigation Solution gently debrided the necrotic tissue, and helped reduce the pain and malodour. Within 6 weeks, the wound was covered with granulation tissue.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
